cial_readme", "decisionReason": "The benchmark results are based on a single run with n_repeats=1, and repeated runs with statistical significance testing are listed as planned next steps, so the scoring contract is not yet stable enough for ongoing comparisons.", "evaluationEvidence": {"reuse": "The leaderboard is written to `results/leaderboard.csv`, and per-repeat results are written to `results/raw_results.csv`. These results come from a single run with n_repeats set to 1.", "scoring": "Fidelity and utility are measured against the holdout set, since that data was never seen by any generator during fitting. Privacy is measured differently: distance to closest record is computed against the training set, because memorization risk concerns the data a generator actually trained on, not data it never saw.", "task": "Three generators are compared: Gaussian Copula, CTGAN (fit on a 25,000 row subsample for 100 epochs to keep CPU runtime reasonable), and an LLM generator built on Groq's openai/gpt-oss-120b model."}, "model": "deepseek-v4-pro", "reviewedAt": "2026-09-11T00:52:53.785364Z", "state": "ai-name-audit-deferred"}, "dataStatus": "primary-source-candidate", "demo": false, "description": "The project evaluates synthetic tabular data generators on fidelity, utility, and privacy metrics using the Give Me Some Credit dataset, comparing Gaussian Copula, CTGAN, and an LLM generator over a fixed evaluation protocol.", "discoverySources": [{"id": "github:mervecaliskann/synthetic-data-benchmark", "type": "github", "url": "https://github.com/Mervecaliskann/synthetic-data-benchmark"}], "displayEligible": false, "domainCuration": {"method": "rules-v1", "state": "auto"}, "evaluationMode": "score_submission", "evidence": {"reasonCodes": ["discovered via github", "benchmark term in abstract", "evaluation protocol evidence", "no explicit benchmark release evidence"], "snippet": "synthetic-data-benchmark Benchmarking synthetic tabular data generators (Gaussian Copula, CTGAN, LLM)